The rejection applies in separate-package mode too. Generating the //plumb:int
provider into a fresh package would emit func int() *app.Server, which happens to
compile in isolation, but naming a set after a predeclared identifier is rejected
uniformly so it can never become a latent shadowing trap once the package gains a
sibling that uses the builtin.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/gen
package-name: gen
error-is: ErrShadowsPredeclared
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

type Server struct{}

//plumb:int
func NewServer() *Server { return &Server{} }
